Carla: draft heads-up — I'm pulling together the release notes for the docs site (aiming to publish tomorrow morning). Included PRs: #4621 (SDK snippet cleanup), #4629 (link redirects), #4635 (changelog bullets). Need a quick sweep on the Known Issues and an engineering-friendly workaround for the streaming oddity.

Jun: on it. I'll reproduce the streaming behavior with the Python and Node samples in #4621. If it's what I think, we should also add a short note to the SDK changelog.

Sam: FYI I patched two redirect targets in #4629. Verified staging: /docs/sdk/py/snippets -> /docs/sdk/python/snippets and /docs/guides/embed -> /docs/guides/embeddings.

Ravi: Observed behavior: when fallback-routing flips between variants mid-stream the client sometimes receives an empty "frame" (zero-length). Workaround snippet: check for empty frames before JSON decode. Example (Node):

```js
// guard against empty streaming chunks
function handleChunk(chunk) {
  if (!chunk || chunk.length === 0) return; // ignore transient empty frame
  try {
    const obj = JSON.parse(chunk);
    // process obj
  } catch (e) {
    // ignore or log parse errors for transient frames
  }
}
```

Carla: thanks @Ravi — adding Node + Python short examples under Known Issues with a link to the SDK issue for the full fix (engineers targeting next minor). Draft summary I'm planning: "Docs release: small UX polish, SDK snippet cleanups, and a couple link fixes. Known streaming edge-case when fallback routing triggers (workaround included)." Thoughts on wording?

Maya: Suggest replacing "small UX polish" with "documentation polish" to avoid confusion with product UX. Also suggest we explicitly label impacted SDKs: (Python, Node).

Jun: +1 to Maya. Also add a quick reproduce step for engineers in the internal ticket: reproduce with seq length > 512 + routing enabled.

Sam: I trimmed one of the bullets to keep the top summary to 3 concise lines: highlights, fixes, known issue + workaround link. Pushed tiny wording PR to draft: #4640.

docs-bot: Merged since last preview: #4621, #4629, #4635. Staging preview URL: https://staging.docs.redwood.ai/release/2026-03-25 (preview expires in 48h).

Carla: perfect. I'll run a final quick-proof in the AM and then publish unless someone flags a problem by 9:00am PT. Please double-check the code fence formatting and that the redirect list matches the staging redirect report. :thumbsup: 

Ravi: added a one-liner note in the draft about expected ETA for a proper runtime fix (next minor release). No blocker from infra.

Jun: proofed and minor clarity edits applied in #4640. All good from my side.

Sam: LGTM, will monitor staging link for any remaining 404s.

Carla: thanks all — publishing tomorrow unless objections.
